# Debian control file — rendered by .github/workflows/release.yml, which
# substitutes the version from quota/version.py for __VERSION__.
Package: quota-manager
Version: __VERSION__
Section: net
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: python3 (>= 3.10), python3-venv, python3-pip, dnsmasq, nftables,
         iproute2, kmod, ppp, ca-certificates
Maintainer: Youssef Alkhodary <youssef.alkhodary@users.noreply.github.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/UserJoo9/QuotaManager
Description: Fair-split metered-internet quota gateway
 Split a metered internet bundle fairly across users and devices. A person's
 allowance covers all their devices; when it runs out every device they own is
 cut at once (a per-device exemption keeps one device online). Per-device and
 per-user speed caps with low-latency fq_codel queues, a dark-purple
 glassmorphism admin dashboard, and a WebSocket live view.
 .
 The gateway needs a wired-NIC laptop running Debian/Kali as root. The package
 configures the network stack (dnsmasq + nftables + tc), installs the Python
 runtime into /opt/quota-manager, and runs the gateway as a systemd service.
